Furnaces, process heat and the material energy account (@th-process-heat: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer, #source "../sources/A-Heat-Transfer-Textbook-Lienhard.lingua#r_7TKQ2D5YRNQ8XVHXNJQDRANWKD", #source "../sources/Advanced-Thermodynamics-MIT-2-43.lingua#r_5GXQQ35FEFJM34SWA12X8QHGKC", #source "../sources/Thermodynamics-and-Chemistry-DeVoe.lingua#r_2YHHGY26Y8X9MS9DB3MXZHD1D1", #thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer "Thermal-response-feedback-and-operating-envelope.lingua#r_4ZNGRXMHDQVHKMC80MZVZ3NDMR", #thermodynamics-and-heat-transfer "../research/Process-temperature-history-product-state-and-heat-recovery.lingua#r_7WQ6CWZ0Q1B9YXXE173P53D5BY") { r_4G1V3TX1T9MJAWBE2TYA17QKXY
**Read:** [A Heat Transfer Textbook — Lienhard and Lienhard](../sources/A-Heat-Transfer-Textbook-Lienhard.lingua#r_7TKQ2D5YRNQ8XVHXNJQDRANWKD), complete enclosure, convection and transient developments; [Advanced Thermodynamics — MIT 2.43, Spring 2024](../sources/Advanced-Thermodynamics-MIT-2-43.lingua#r_5GXQQ35FEFJM34SWA12X8QHGKC), exergy and whole-process accounting; [Thermodynamics and Chemistry — Howard DeVoe](../sources/Thermodynamics-and-Chemistry-DeVoe.lingua#r_2YHHGY26Y8X9MS9DB3MXZHD1D1), reaction and phase-change energies.

A furnace or process heater serves a material transformation, drying duty or controlled thermal history. Draw the material and energy streams, define reactions and phase changes, and separate energy reaching the product from exhaust, enclosure, opening and cooling losses. A useful-product definition must accompany an efficiency.

Couple enclosure radiation, gas/surface exchange, conduction into the load and its changing properties. Include the time needed to reach a required internal condition rather than controlling only the chamber temperature. A uniform wall temperature does not imply a uniform moving product.

Connect the account with [Industrial chemistry — chemical transformations, useful products and continuing production](../../../chemistry/industrial-chemistry/Industrial-chemistry.lingua#r_3AKBAFB2ABJ0671QW6ZBQ0B618) and [Metals and metallurgical production — feed, refining, structure, useful products, and recovery](../../../materials/metals-and-metallurgical-production/Metals-and-metallurgical-production.lingua#r_59BDAQXT81552YF5F8TH4KQQH1) for actual process chemistry and material transformations. Compare an improved insulation, heat-recovery or scheduling proposal at equal product requirements and throughput. Include measurement uncertainty and the ability to sustain the proposed boundary conditions; a theoretical reduction in heat input is not yet demonstrated product quality or plant performance.

**Continue:** [Thermal response, feedback and the operating envelope](Thermal-response-feedback-and-operating-envelope.lingua#r_4ZNGRXMHDQVHKMC80MZVZ3NDMR) · [Advanced study: process thermal history and heat recovery](../research/Process-temperature-history-product-state-and-heat-recovery.lingua#r_7WQ6CWZ0Q1B9YXXE173P53D5BY).

